    "problem_statement": "QR code generation produces incorrect version numbers\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen generating QR codes, the library is producing QR codes with higher version numbers than expected. This affects both optimized and non-optimized data encoding modes.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport qrcode\nfrom qrcode.constants import MODE_ALPHA_NUM, MODE_NUMBER\n\n# Test with alphanumeric data\nqr = qrcode.QRCode()\nqr.add_data('ABCDEFGHIJ1234567890', optimize=0)\nqr.make()\nprint(f\"Expected version: 1, Got version: {qr.version}\")\n\n# Test with numeric data  \nqr = qrcode.QRCode()\nqr.add_data('1234567890123456789012345678901234', optimize=0)\nqr.make()\nprint(f\"Expected version: 1, Got version: {qr.version}\")\n\n# Test with mixed data and optimization\ntext = 'A1abc12345123451234512345def1HELLOHELLOHELLOHELLOa' * 5\nqr = qrcode.QRCode()\nqr.add_data(text)\nqr.make()\nprint(f\"Expected version: 10, Got version: {qr.version}\")\n```\n\nExpected output:\n```\nExpected version: 1, Got version: 1\nExpected version: 1, Got version: 1\nExpected version: 10, Got version: 10\n```\n\nActual output:\n```\nExpected version: 1, Got version: 2\nExpected version: 1, Got version: 2\nExpected version: 10, Got version: 11\n```\n\nThe QR codes are being generated with version numbers that are one higher than they should be, which means they're using more space than necessary for the given data."
